# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BLASTI Desktop App — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file documents ALL environment variables used by the Electron desktop app.
# Copy this to .env and fill in your values.
#
# NOTE: The desktop app is an Electron shell that loads the web app.
# Most configuration comes from the web app it connects to.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── CONNECTION (the one setting that matters for VPS deploys) ────────
# The CLOUD ORIGIN the desktop app talks to for login, sync and realtime —
# the machine that actually serves /api/* and /socket.io/* (apps/api, the
# Hono server, usually behind a reverse proxy). The UI itself is always
# served locally by the embedded local API, so this is the ONLY URL you
# normally need to set.
#
# ⚠️ ORIGIN ONLY — NEVER append a path (this is the #1 misconfiguration):
#   ✅ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="http://203.0.113.227"        (raw IP, HTTP testing)
#   ✅ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="https://blasti.example.com"  (domain + HTTPS)
#   ❌ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="http://203.0.113.227/api"    → app probes
#      /api/api/health → 404 → "cloud unreachable". The app appends
#      /api/* ITSELF. (Newer builds auto-strip the suffix with a warning.)
#
# HOW .env IS LOADED (Electron does NOT read .env by itself — BLASTI does,
# see load-env.js / main.js; first match wins, OS environment overrides):
#   1. OS environment variables      (runtime override, advanced use)
#   2. <install>\resources\.env      (packaged app — EDITABLE AFTER INSTALL
#       without rebuilding, e.g.
#       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\BLASTI\resources\.env on Windows)
#   3. apps/desktop/.env             (baked into the installer at build time)
#   4. project root .env             (DEV MODE ONLY — BLASTI_* keys ONLY;
#       lets you keep the VPS URL next to the web/api vars you already have
#       in the monorepo root .env. All other root keys are ignored by the
#       desktop app so cloud secrets never leak into it.)
#   5. build-stamp.json              (Task 74 — the cloud URL the BUILD
#       machine was configured with is baked into every packaged build)
#   6. built-in default              (packaged: the production VPS, currently
#       http://68.183.137.227 — same server the release APK is locked to.
#       Dev runs keep the http://localhost:3003 default.)
#
# The EFFECTIVE cloud URL is printed once at startup:
#   [BLASTI Desktop] Cloud API → https://…  [source: …]
# If you see "[source: built-in default — NO cloud URL configured]" (dev runs
# only) the app keeps using localhost:3003 until you set the variable in one
# of the places above and restart. Packaged builds instead print
# "[source: baked at build time (build-stamp.json)]" or
# "[source: packaged production default (VPS)]".
#
# FOR A VPS DEPLOYMENT (dev / electron:dev) — either create
#   apps/desktop/.env        with:  BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="https://blasti.example.com"
# or add the same line to the PROJECT ROOT .env (picked up automatically).
# For an INSTALLED app edit <install>\resources\.env instead — no rebuild needed.
#
# Do NOT point it at a static web host — it must be the origin that
# actually serves the /api/* routes.
#
# BLASTI_API_URL is accepted as a legacy alias with LOWER precedence:
# BLASTI_CLOUD_URL > BLASTI_API_URL > build-stamp > packaged VPS default.
# BLASTI_API_URL="https://blasti.example.com"

# ─── LOCAL DATABASE (single authoritative location) ─────────────────
# Optional override. Default (recommended): <userData>/blasti-local/local.db
# i.e. %APPDATA%/@blasti/desktop/blasti-local/local.db on Windows.
# Legacy databases at ~/.blasti/local are auto-migrated (copied + verified)
# to the authoritative path at first startup — the old file is kept as backup.
# BLASTI_LOCAL_DB_DIR=""

# ─── LAN SERVER ─────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins for the LAN server (port 3080).
# This controls which devices on the local network can connect.
# Development: "http://localhost:3000"
# Production: "http://192.168.1.100:3000,http://192.168.1.50:3000"
# BLASTI_LAN_ORIGINS="http://localhost:3000"

# ─── AUTHENTICATION ──────────────────────────────────
# Secret for JWT signing on the LAN server.
# Should match NEXTAUTH_SECRET from the web/API .env files.
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET="blast1-dev-s3cr3t-k3y-f0r-d3v3l0pm3nt-0nly"

# ─── DEVELOPMENT ─────────────────────────────────────
# Set ELECTRON_DEV=1 or pass --dev flag to run in development mode.
# This loads http://localhost:3000 instead of the production URL.
# ELECTRON_DEV="1"
# NODE_ENV="development"
